  \bibinfo {note} {The envelope function refers to a mathematical
  representation of a wavefunction in quantum wells, characterized by a plane
  wave in the in-plane directions (x, y) and a localized wavefunction in the
  z-direction, normalized to the sample area. It describes the spatial
  distribution of particles confined in a quantum system while allowing for
  extended states in the unconfined directions \cite
